From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:49:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: translate fcanonicalize, and name an untranslated ALU op
 in the MSL

nir_opt_algebraic turns x * 1.0, x + -0.0, fmin(x, x), fneg(fneg(x))
and the like into fcanonicalize. It removes every fcanonicalize unless
the shader flushes denormals of that size, or the result is used only
as a float. KosmicKrisp reports no flush-to-zero mode
(shaderDenormFlushToZeroFloat16/32 false), but spirv_to_nir takes a
DenormFlushToZero execution mode with only a warning. vkd3d-proton
declares FP32 flush-to-zero when a driver reports it; replayed under a
profile that does, 297 of Red Dead Redemption 2's 3,564 DX12 MSL
libraries had an fcanonicalize whose result is stored as bits.

alu_to_msl had no case for it. Its default printed "ALU <op>", with no
operand, into the MSL, and Apple's Metal compiler rejects every such
library ("expected ';' after expression"). Translate fcanonicalize as
its source: Metal has no canonicalize, and no reported mode asks for
the flush. The default now prints "Unknown ALU <op>", like an unknown
intrinsic's "Unknown intrinsic <name>": it is still not valid MSL, so
the library fails to compile and the pipeline fails to build, and the
text names what was missing.

No other ALU op is left untranslated by KosmicKrisp's lowering for the
features it reports: the rest are other drivers' ops, are produced only
under compiler options KosmicKrisp does not set, are lowered by those it
sets, or come only from OpenCL or from features it does not report
(64-bit floats, bfloat16, 8-bit floats, Intel integer functions 2).

Mesa main (9a1e58da, checked on 2026-10-18) has neither change.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-rdr2-vulkan-needs.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
index 63d2ec12..274823e3 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -616,6 +616,12 @@ alu_to_msl(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_alu_instr *instr)
       alu_src_to_msl(ctx, instr, 0);
       break;
    case nir_op_mov:
+   /* fcanonicalize flushes denormals only under a flush-to-zero float mode,
+    * and nir_opt_algebraic removes it in every other shader. KosmicKrisp
+    * reports no flush-to-zero mode, so a shader that declares one anyway
+    * (spirv_to_nir accepts it with a warning) gets its source unchanged:
+    * Metal has no canonicalize. */
+   case nir_op_fcanonicalize:
       alu_src_to_msl(ctx, instr, 0);
       break;
    case nir_op_b2f32:
@@ -634,7 +640,9 @@ alu_to_msl(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_alu_instr *instr)
       alu_src_to_msl(ctx, instr, 2);
       break;
    default:
-      P(ctx, "ALU %s", nir_op_infos[instr->op].name);
+      /* Not valid MSL, so the library fails to compile and the pipeline
+       * fails to build, as with an unknown intrinsic. */
+      P(ctx, "Unknown ALU %s", nir_op_infos[instr->op].name);
    }
 }
 
